KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp26 --object-bits 12 --unwind 4 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ full at its capacity: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
std::inplace_vector ([inplace.vector]).  With GCC 16's headers CBMC failed
to parse <utility> in C++26 mode (std::constant_wrapper::operator[]
expands a pack in a subscript, cpp23_subscript_pack_expansion_forms), and
it preprocessed C++26 as C++23, so <inplace_vector> was empty.  N5008's
try_push_back returns a pointer, GCC 16's an optional<T&> (a later
revision); the test uses neither type.  Checked with GCC 16.
